es_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/commit/ddebc72255212c808db21d146078b3b3f5897038 breaks local docker platform resolution\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\nHere is an example run:\r\nbazel clean && bazel run --experimental_remote_platform_override='properties:{ name:\"container-image\" value:\"docker://gcr.io/cloud-marketplace/google/rbe-ubuntu16-04@sha256:59bf0e191a6b5cc1ab62c2224c810681d1326bad5a27b1d36c9f40113e79da7f\" }' --spawn_strategy=docker --define=EXECUTOR=remote --crosstool_top=@bazel_toolchains_test_suite_repo//configs/ubuntu16_04_clang/1.0/bazel_0.13.0/default:toolchain --experimental_enable_docker_sandbox :hello-world\r\n\r\nThis works with bazel pre-ddebc72255212c808db21d146078b3b3f5897038 but after fails with the message:\r\n\r\nCannot execute CppCompile mnemonic with Docker, because no image could be found in the remote_execution_properties of the platform and no default image was set via --experimental_docker_image\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nRodette\r\n\r\n### If `bazel info release` returns \"development version\" or \"(@non-git)\", tell us how you built Bazel.\r\n\r\nCompiled from source at above commit\r\n\r\n### Any other information, logs, or outputs that you want to share?\r\n\r\nI don't think the contents matter, but here's my hello_world.cc:\r\n#include <iostream>\r\n#include <unistd.h>\r\n\r\nint main(int argc, char** argv) {\r\n  std::cout << \"Hello, world! 22224446667778889990000123444A12\" << std::endl;\r\n  sleep(1);\r\n  std::cerr << \"Howdy!!\" << std::endl;\r\n  return 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\nAnd BUILD:\r\ncc_binary(\r\n    name = \"hello-world\",\r\n    srcs = [\"hello-world.cc\"],\r\n)","